3. Top 5 English Interview Questions & Bullet Answers on Value Functions:

   Q1. What is the difference between LAG() and LEAD()?
   Ans: LAG() fetches data from a previous row, while LEAD() fetches data from a subsequent row.

   Q2. Why did the first row of LAG() and the last row of LEAD() return NULL?
   Ans: Because there is no row before the first row, and no row after the last row to fetch data from.

   Q3. Why is LAST_VALUE() changing per row instead of showing 700 for all?
   Ans: Because the default window frame is "RANGE BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW". It only looks up to the current row.

   Q4. How do you fix LAST_VALUE() to return the absolute last value (700) for every row?
   Ans: Add "ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING" to the OVER clause.

   Q5. What is the default offset value for LEAD() and LAG() if not specified?
   Ans: 1 row.


